247
00:11:46.444 --> 00:11:49.364
- Well. I didn't ask for a favor.
- Sometimes you don't need to ask.

248
00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.085
Got a passport.

249
00:11:52.577 --> 00:11:55.448
This guy's been to countries
I haven't even heard of.

250
00:11:58.092 --> 00:11:59.040
What is this?

251
00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.380
I don't know.

252
00:12:03.277 --> 00:12:05.005
It's something you're familiar with?

253
00:12:05.325 --> 00:12:07.465
Foreign currency. lots of it.

254
00:12:10.783 --> 00:12:13.742
Booth found this in tall.
dark and handsome's drawer.

255
00:12:14.323 --> 00:12:16.000
It's an RF proximity card.

256
00:12:16.125 --> 00:12:17.548
And that would be...?

257
00:12:17.673 --> 00:12:20.043
Basically. it's a
super fancy key card.

258
00:12:20.168 --> 00:12:24.374
You wave the card in front of the reader
it logs your infoand the door opens.

259
00:12:24.499 --> 00:12:26.669
Any way to figure out
what door it opens?

260
00:12:26.794 --> 00:12:30.697
Well. if the info on the card
isn't too heavily encrypted.

261
00:12:30.865 --> 00:12:33.908
I heard you tried to get Hodgins
interested in doing an experiment.

262
00:12:34.272 --> 00:12:36.036
Let's just say I planted the seed.

263
00:12:40.668 --> 00:12:42.738
- What? CIA? NSA?
- No.

264
00:12:43.473 --> 00:12:44.758
Dupont Circle.

265
00:13:10.359 --> 00:13:11.974
Special Agent Booth. FBI.

266
00:13:17.668 --> 00:13:19.295
Welcome to the Woodbury School.

267
00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.185
How are you?
What's with all the security?

268
00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:24.344
It's precautionary. Our student body
includes chdren of diplomats.

269
00:13:24.469 --> 00:13:26.489
heads of state. CEOs.

270
00:13:27.423 --> 00:13:29.994
- How old is your child?
- Parker? He's seven.

271
00:13:30.395 --> 00:13:32.967
- Has he been evaluated?
- He does just fine.

272
00:13:33.137 --> 00:13:36.242
Most applicant families engage
an educational consultant.

273
00:13:36.503 --> 00:13:38.395
It's not a requirement.
of course. but...

274
00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.938
Mr. Donnegan. I think you got this
l wrong.

275
00:13:41.139 --> 00:13:43.458
I know it seems crazy.
but given the demand.

276
00:13:43.583 --> 00:13:46.353
we can only accept the
most qualified applicants.

277
00:13:46.796 --> 00:13:48.247
Parker's a great kid.

278
00:13:49.482 --> 00:13:51.569
The problem is keeping him
that way. isn't it?

279
00:13:51.739 --> 00:13:55.115
68% of our students matriculate
to Ivy League universities.

280
00:13:55.283 --> 00:13:58.717
And it's not because of
our electron microscope or AP classes.

281
00:13:59.662 --> 00:14:01.496
It's because of our Honor Code.

282
00:14:02.081 --> 00:14:04.582
Any violation results
in immediate dismissal.

283
00:14:05.303 --> 00:14:07.168
Why don't I get you
an admissions packet?

284
00:14:07.338 --> 00:14:08.680
Actually. I'm...

285
00:14:09.777 --> 00:14:11.756
I'm here because of
a murder investigation.

286
00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:15.135
- I'm sorry?
- One of your parking access cards

287
00:14:15.303 --> 00:14:18.430
was found in the apartment
of a victim. Cal Warren.

288
00:14:19.595 --> 00:14:22.642
He's not a parent or an employee.
I would know the name.

289
00:14:23.346 --> 00:14:26.021
- Maybe we can check your computer.
- Of course.

290
00:14:26.953 --> 00:14:30.032
No one is issued a key card
without security clearance.

291
00:14:30.543 --> 00:14:31.503
Thanks.

292
00:14:31.628 --> 00:14:34.866
One of our fathers actually implemented
the security system.

293
00:14:35.221 --> 00:14:37.526
He's deputy director of the CIA.

294
00:14:38.351 --> 00:14:39.210
Really?

295
00:14:42.969 --> 00:14:44.780
There he is. Calvin Warren.

296
00:14:45.333 --> 00:14:46.833
Did he happen to work for the CIA?

297
00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:49.335
No. actually.
he works for the president.

298
00:14:49.505 --> 00:14:50.795
Of the United States?

299
00:14:51.993 --> 00:14:53.454
Parents Association.

300
00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.675
As a nanny.

301
00:14:56.038 --> 00:14:57.039
A nanny?

302
00:15:04.467 --> 00:15:06.352
28 grand a year.

303
00:15:06.522 --> 00:15:08.379
I didn't pay that much
for 4 years of college.

304
00:15:08.504 --> 00:15:11.171
If you think it's so ridiculous.
why did you save the application?

305
00:15:11.296 --> 00:15:14.152
I didn't save it. I just didn't have
a chance to throw it out yet.

306
00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:15.939
You don't have to be embarrassed.

307
00:15:16.064 --> 00:15:18.656
It's perfectly normal
to want the best for Parker.

308
00:15:18.826 --> 00:15:21.409
Public school was good enough for me.
it's good enough for my kid.

309
00:15:21.579 --> 00:15:23.286
Of course it is. Probably.

310
00:15:24.834 --> 00:15:26.456
What's that supposed to mean?

311
00:15:27.898 --> 00:15:30.748
Parker is a bright.
engaged little boy.

312
00:15:30.873 --> 00:15:33.505
I'm sure he'll do fine
in a large classroom.

313
00:15:34.117 --> 00:15:35.798
- I did.
- Except...

314
00:15:36.801 --> 00:15:39.248
- Except what?
- Your dad was a science teacher.

315
00:15:39.373 --> 00:15:40.553
You're a scientist.

316
00:15:40.805 --> 00:15:43.393
Yes. my education was
enriched at home.

317
00:15:43.726 --> 00:15:46.926
That's what I got to do.
Enrich Parker at home.

318
00:15:49.025 --> 00:15:52.204
In what academics
are you qualified to offer enrichment?

319
00:15:53.084 --> 00:15:53.852
Well...

320
00:16:05.788 --> 00:16:07.962
Ethe could you grab my bag. please?

321
00:16:08.087 --> 00:16:10.541
I am on my way to the
Children First board meeting.

322
00:16:10.711 --> 00:16:11.751
Thank you.

323
00:16:12.091 --> 00:16:13.711
Wexler has the groomer at three.

324
00:16:14.328 --> 00:16:16.756
- Excuse me. Elisbeth King?
- Yes?

325
00:16:17.061 --> 00:16:18.132
We're the FBI.

326
00:16:18.965 --> 00:16:20.718
Do you know a Mr. Calvin Warren?

327
00:16:21.402 --> 00:16:22.428
He was my nanny.

328
00:16:23.235 --> 00:16:25.762
- What happened?
- That's what we're investigating.

329
00:16:26.908 --> 00:16:29.018
Cal dropped off the face
of the earth on Sunday.

330
00:16:29.878 --> 00:16:31.354
He was an excellent nanny.

331
00:16:31.626 --> 00:16:34.329
Well. how is it that
an ex-Special Ops guy

332
00:16:34.855 --> 00:16:35.907
becomes a nanny?

333
00:16:36.032 --> 00:16:37.985
My husband. Richard.
handles defense contracts.

334
00:16:38.318 --> 00:16:39.828
The Middle East. South America.

335
00:16:39.953 --> 00:16:42.746
There were kidnap threats
a couple years ago. he was concerned.

336
00:16:42.871 --> 00:16:44.534
He offered Cal $2.500 a week.

337
00:16:44.945 --> 00:16:46.661
That's very good pay for

338
00:16:47.013 --> 00:16:48.022
a babysitter.

339
00:16:48.147 --> 00:16:50.032
Cal was more like a bodyguard.

340
00:16:50.157 --> 00:16:51.694
That's what got him killed?

341
00:16:51.819 --> 00:16:53.417
Someone after my children?

342
00:16:55.339 --> 00:16:56.921
Could we speak to your children?

343
00:16:57.367 --> 00:16:58.313
Of course.

344
00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:04.059
Okay. so what time on Sunday
did you last see Cal?

345
00:17:04.668 --> 00:17:06.562
- Why?
- Because it's pertinent

346
00:17:06.687 --> 00:17:08.057
to our investigation.

347
00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:11.561
- Wei shen me ta wen zhe ge wen ti?
- Bu zhi dao.

348
00:17:11.686 --> 00:17:13.474
- What?
- Mandarin Chinese.

349
00:17:13.682 --> 00:17:16.818
My father says the Chinese will
run the planet in ten years.

350
00:17:17.119 --> 00:17:18.805
He figures it'll be useful.

351
00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.154
- That's very smart.
- Okay. well. here. today.

352
00:17:21.279 --> 00:17:22.822
okay. I run the world.

353
00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:25.366
Bun tyen-shung duh ee-dway ro.

354
00:17:26.581 --> 00:17:29.043
He just called you a stupid.
inbred stack of meat.

355
00:17:29.168 --> 00:17:30.299
Really?

356
00:17:30.998 --> 00:17:33.249
I'm sorry. do you ha
something to say to me?

357
00:17:36.104 --> 00:17:38.075
Dui bu qi. Xie xie.

358
00:17:38.983 --> 00:17:40.214
He. he apologized.

359
00:17:40.658 --> 00:17:43.092
Good. So. you want to tell me
what happened on Sunday?

360
00:17:44.337 --> 00:17:47.014
Well. Cal dropped me off at
the algebra tutor around 8:00.

361
00:17:47.139 --> 00:17:48.890
then took Lexie
to check out a new horse.

362
00:17:49.058 --> 00:17:51.142
In the afternoon. you had
a game against All Saints.

363
00:17:51.435 --> 00:17:53.304
Lacrosse. I got this.

364
00:17:54.472 --> 00:17:55.598
Let's see.

365
00:17:56.145 --> 00:17:57.939
And Cal took you
to the emergency room?

366
00:17:58.064 --> 00:18:00.327
No. He knew one of the moms
was a doctor. so

367
00:18:00.452 --> 00:18:01.903
he figured she'd do a better job.

368
00:18:02.071 --> 00:18:03.863
Looks like the work
of a plastic surgeon.

369
00:18:04.031 --> 00:18:05.326
No. dermatologist.

370
00:18:05.621 --> 00:18:06.657
Dr. Ezralow.

371
00:18:07.591 --> 00:18:08.851
Very competent.

372
00:18:11.868 --> 00:18:14.054
The Royce boy was stitched up
by the same doctor

373
00:18:14.179 --> 00:18:16.458
who said she didn't know Cal Warren.

374
00:18:16.583 --> 00:18:18.628
I'm having her
brought in for questioning.

375
00:18:18.869 --> 00:18:20.963
You think those kids
are better off than Parker?

376
00:18:21.088 --> 00:18:22.256
Of course they are.

377
00:18:22.573 --> 00:18:25.027
They have every advantage:
a wonderful school.

378
00:18:25.152 --> 00:18:27.637
a successful father. mother
committed to charity work.

379
00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.669
I spend more time with my houseplants
than they do with their kids.

380
00:18:32.269 --> 00:18:34.857
Children of privilege have
always been raised by staff.

381
00:18:34.982 --> 00:18:37.429
It's how the upper one percent
stays the upper one percent.

382
00:18:37.554 --> 00:18:41.889
Assuming quality education
and adequate supervision.

383
00:18:42.014 --> 00:18:44.570
parents are actually rather
irrelevant beyond a certain age.

384
00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.936
- You're kidding me.
- Look at this.

385
00:18:47.061 --> 00:18:50.117
They start Latin in third grade.
That's fantastic.

386
00:18:50.287 --> 00:18:52.845
No. You know what's more important
than academic enrichment?

387
00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.587
A loving environment.
You ask anyone.

388
00:18:54.712 --> 00:18:58.209
Parker is a wonderful child. Booth.
You shouldn't feel inadequate.

389
00:18:58.377 --> 00:19:00.419
I'm perfectly
capable of raising my own kid.

390
00:19:01.668 --> 00:19:03.839
- You're being defensive.
- I am not.

391
00:19:04.009 --> 00:19:05.601
It's because
you only have one child.

392
00:19:05.726 --> 00:19:07.927
When you procreate in multiples.
there's less pressure.

393
00:19:08.095 --> 00:19:10.721
Thank you. I feel much better.

394
00:19:15.808 --> 00:19:16.901
This way.

395
00:19:17.481 --> 00:19:18.582
Have a seat.

396
00:19:18.707 --> 00:19:20.410
I apologize. Agent Booth.

397
00:19:20.535 --> 00:19:23.722
When you called and asked
if I knew a Calvin Warren.

398
00:19:24.456 --> 00:19:26.862
I just didn't put it together
with the King's nanny.

399
00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.097
- So you did know him?
- Yes. But just as Cal.

400
00:19:29.222 --> 00:19:32.618
My son is on the same
lacrosse team as the King boy.

401
00:19:32.788 --> 00:19:34.479
Did you have
any more dealings with him?

402
00:19:34.604 --> 00:19:36.110
I'm afraid not.

403
00:19:36.859 --> 00:19:39.959
Actually. no. that's not true.
I'm sorry. again.

404
00:19:40.127 --> 00:19:41.739
Calvin came along with us one time

405
00:19:41.864 --> 00:19:44.046
when I took the.
King children up for a ride.

406
00:19:45.058 --> 00:19:46.852
- A ride?
- I'm a pilot.

407
00:19:47.315 --> 00:19:48.718
I own a Senecaive.

408
00:19:49.143 --> 00:19:50.733
Cal got sick. and. well.

409
00:19:50.858 --> 00:19:52.680
the boys thought that was hilarious.

410
00:19:52.848 --> 00:19:54.736
You wouldn't happen
to know how Cal Warren

411
00:19:54.861 --> 00:19:56.767
got a prescription
for painkillers from you?

412
00:19:57.733 --> 00:19:59.272
Isn't that obvious?

413
00:19:59.673 --> 00:20:02.770
That's why he brought Royce King
to me to be stitched up.

414
00:20:03.896 --> 00:20:05.691
To steal my prescription pad.

415
00:20:08.782 --> 00:20:11.279
I have no further questions.
so. thanks for coming in.

416
00:20:11.404 --> 00:20:14.035
I feel stupid for not being able
to put the face with the name.

417
00:20:14.203 --> 00:20:17.249
- I'm so sorry for wasting your time.
- No worries. Have a nice day.

418
00:20:20.684 --> 00:20:24.225
So you know that thing where you insist
that all information goes through you?

419
00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:26.615
Yes. and I'm afraid I'm
immovable on the subject.

420
00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:29.695
And you send out little e-mails
summarizing the case so far?

421
00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:32.615
Yes. plus I check those e-mails
to see if they've been opened.

422
00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:34.905
- That's a very good system.
- Thank you.

423
00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:37.724
Because if you weren't checking.
I probably never would have read

424
00:20:37.849 --> 00:20:40.505
the e-mail that said Booth
questioned a flying dermatologist.

425
00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.770
I hope you're not trying
to get some free lotion.

426
00:20:42.895 --> 00:20:45.425
I ran the accelerant sample
through the GC mass spec.

427
00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.764
There were traces
of tetra-ethyl lead.

428
00:20:48.246 --> 00:20:49.808
- Have we changed the subject?
- No.

429
00:20:49.933 --> 00:20:51.789
if you hadn't been
so anal about the e-mails.

430
00:20:51.914 --> 00:20:54.910
I never would've known that I discovered
something that wasn't merely interesting

431
00:20:55.035 --> 00:20:56.493
but vital to the investigation.

432
00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.370
Which is tetra ethyl lead?

433
00:20:58.495 --> 00:21:01.130
Tetra-ethyl lead was a common
antiknock additive in gasoline

434
00:21:01.255 --> 00:21:04.168
that went out with catalytic
converters and unleaded gas.

435
00:21:04.337 --> 00:21:06.533
Does the flying dermatologist
drive a vintage car?

436
00:21:06.658 --> 00:21:09.465
Maybe. But for sure. the flying
dermatologist flies a plane.

437
00:21:10.142 --> 00:21:11.217
Aviation gas?

438
00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:14.470
The victim's remains were
incinerated by aviation gas.

439
00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.355
I'll let Booth know.

440
00:21:16.571 --> 00:21:19.967
Hopefully. she hasn't flown the coop
while you were getting to the point.

441
00:21:20.241 --> 00:21:22.311
I was just trying to be nice.

442
00:21:28.408 --> 00:21:30.177
- You lied to me.
- Yes.

443
00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:32.571
I wrote Cal a prescription
for painkillers.

444
00:21:33.176 --> 00:21:34.427
I shouldn't have.

445
00:21:34.784 --> 00:21:37.028
- That's the truth.
- Yeah. but not this time. Doc.

446
00:21:37.153 --> 00:21:39.275
Now that I know that
you're a world-class liar.

447
00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.796
I came just a little bit
more prepared this time.

448
00:21:43.892 --> 00:21:45.395
Take a look at that there.

449
00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.002
My flight logs...

450
00:21:47.172 --> 00:21:49.171
- for the past year.
- Yeah.

451
00:21:49.341 --> 00:21:51.841
Oh. looky here. this one here.

452
00:21:52.009 --> 00:21:53.145
Right here.

453
00:21:54.655 --> 00:21:56.512
Yes. I took Cal flying a few times.

454
00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.035
Without the kids?

455
00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.580
This one here is my favorite.

456
00:22:01.705 --> 00:22:03.860
This particular flight to New York.

457
00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.989
You were gone the whole weekend.

458
00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:12.798
All right.

459
00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:15.935
All right. I'll tell you
what you want to know.

460
00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:19.493
No. my husband didn't know I was
having an affair with the Kings'manny.

461
00:22:20.203 --> 00:22:22.621
Would I have killed Cal to
prevent him from finding out?

462
00:22:22.801 --> 00:22:24.207
No. I would not.

463
00:22:26.354 --> 00:22:27.172
Why?

464
00:22:27.504 --> 00:22:30.665
Because my husband doesn't
give a damn who I boff.

465
00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:34.425
Do I know anyone else
who might wish Cal ill?

466
00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:36.072
Yes.

467
00:22:36.517 --> 00:22:37.511
Richard King.

468
00:22:38.519 --> 00:22:40.890
Don't stop. this is great.
Keep going.

469
00:22:41.355 --> 00:22:43.308
Cal told me to sell a stock.

470
00:22:43.725 --> 00:22:47.405
He said he had some insider knowledge
that. this company was in trouble.

471
00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:49.482
I took the tip. made a killing.

472
00:22:49.650 --> 00:22:51.775
That's when I flew him to
New York to say thank you.

473
00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:55.559
And he said "you're
welcome" all weekend.

474
00:22:57.534 --> 00:22:59.408
What's this have to
do with Richard King?

475
00:23:01.187 --> 00:23:03.412
It was Richard King's company.

476
00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:13.868
- How's that look. Max?
- Good. looks good.

477
00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:16.720
Never thought I'd be
doing another experiment.

478
00:23:17.145 --> 00:23:18.827
Dad. what are you doing in here?

479
00:23:18.952 --> 00:23:20.896
Max had a great idea
for an experiment.

480
00:23:21.655 --> 00:23:24.165
Dad. you said you
wouldn't touch evidence.

481
00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:26.280
He's been very careful not to
touch the evidence.

482
00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:29.279
You know. your old man. he reminded
me why I got into science.

483
00:23:29.668 --> 00:23:31.355
- To catch murderers?
- No.

484
00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:33.450
To figure stuff out in amusing ways.

485
00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:36.515
The bones were incinerated
by aviation fuel.

486
00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.414
They just need to know. uh. how
strong the wind was basic.

487
00:23:39.584 --> 00:23:41.935
So. figure out how big
a wind blew the bones...

488
00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:43.491
Check the weather charts.

489
00:23:43.616 --> 00:23:45.327
Basic. that's very basic.

490
00:23:46.049 --> 00:23:48.799
But this is the same wind tunnel you
helped me build for the science fair.

491
00:23:48.967 --> 00:23:50.634
Right. a basic wind tunnel. honey.

492
00:23:51.271 --> 00:23:52.719
You won first prize.

493
00:23:53.021 --> 00:23:55.764
I made casts that weigh the same
as the bones we found in that tree.

494
00:23:55.934 --> 00:23:57.474
All right. now...

495
00:23:58.220 --> 00:24:00.527
we put the skull cast
into the wind tunnel

496
00:24:00.652 --> 00:24:02.896
since that
was the largest artifact on the tree.

497
00:24:04.192 --> 00:24:05.889
I didn't touch anything.

498
00:24:06.693 --> 00:24:11.029
The bone begins to move at wind
speeds of 42 miles per hour.

499
00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:14.157
Not enough net force to
achieve aerodynamic lift.

500
00:24:14.410 --> 00:24:16.201
But crank it to 69...

501
00:24:23.516 --> 00:24:25.802
I checked the National Weather Service.
There were windstorms

502
00:24:25.927 --> 00:24:27.120
in that area last week.

503
00:24:27.245 --> 00:24:30.716
A strong nor'easter hit 71
miles per hour late last Tuesday.

504
00:24:30.884 --> 00:24:34.377
That gives us a 48-hour window
for Calvin Warren's murder.

505
00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:37.304
We still don't know where he was
killed or where the body was dumped.

506
00:24:37.429 --> 00:24:39.954
- Wait a minute. I can figure that out.
- Dad. you're fired.

507
00:24:40.079 --> 00:24:40.842
What?

508
00:24:40.967 --> 00:24:44.730
The National Oceanic and
Atmospheric Administration.

509
00:24:44.898 --> 00:24:46.565
The NOAA tracks surface conditions.

510
00:24:46.733 --> 00:24:50.815
We can calculate where the bones started
out if we can plot approximate mass

511
00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:53.010
and reverse the path
of that nor'easterly.

512
00:24:53.135 --> 00:24:56.206
The heavier remains will still
be near the original dump site.

513
00:24:57.187 --> 00:25:00.662
- You see. I'm helping.
- Oh. most definitely is helping.

514
00:25:00.990 --> 00:25:02.777
I'm sorry. Dad. but you're fired.

515
00:25:02.902 --> 00:25:05.443
You took part
in a forensic experiment.

516
00:25:05.568 --> 00:25:08.295
You said you wouldn't. but
you did. so now you're fired.

517
00:25:08.860 --> 00:25:10.453
He didn't touch any of the evidence.

518
00:25:10.578 --> 00:25:11.738
It's okay. kid.

519
00:25:12.414 --> 00:25:13.507
Never mind.

520
00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:19.931
Nice assist. Mick.

521
00:25:20.099 --> 00:25:21.835
Now take him out quick.

522
00:25:22.750 --> 00:25:23.737
No. Mick!

523
00:25:24.830 --> 00:25:26.144
Pass it! Pass it!

524
00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:28.106
Hi. Alexa. How are you?

525
00:25:28.274 --> 00:25:31.755
Shouldn't you be like. studying algebra.
Chinese or solving the world's problems?

526
00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:33.320
I'm cheering for Royce.

527
00:25:33.740 --> 00:25:35.173
He's the goalie.

528
00:25:36.817 --> 00:25:39.237
I watch football.
It's a better sport. It's American.

529
00:25:39.362 --> 00:25:42.005
Lacrosse was invented
by the American Indian.

530
00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:44.595
You can't get much
more American than that.

531
00:25:47.374 --> 00:25:49.169
- Oh. God. what now?
- I'm thinking about

532
00:25:49.294 --> 00:25:50.754
this whole insider trading thing.

533
00:25:50.922 --> 00:25:52.229
I told you everything.

534
00:25:52.465 --> 00:25:54.324
I'm thinking Cal
gives you a tip on a stock.

535
00:25:54.449 --> 00:25:56.264
you sell it.
you make $2 million.$3 million.

536
00:25:56.389 --> 00:25:57.935
it raises questions in my mind.

537
00:25:58.060 --> 00:26:02.057
How did Richard King find out
that Cal spilled insider knowledge?

538
00:26:02.230 --> 00:26:03.475
That's right. Bones.

539
00:26:04.003 --> 00:26:04.935
I don't know.

540
00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:08.397
Well. where were you between
last Sunday and Tuesday night?

541
00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:10.495
- Who is she?
- Don't get jealous. Doc.

542
00:26:10.620 --> 00:26:12.351
Just answer the question.

543
00:26:12.992 --> 00:26:14.294
I was in San Antonio

544
00:26:14.419 --> 00:26:17.030
doing skin grafts on a firefighter
with third-degree burns.

545
00:26:17.273 --> 00:26:19.462
- You've got your own plane.
- You had time to fly back.

546
00:26:19.587 --> 00:26:22.738
You really want me to believe
that Richard King killed Cal.

547
00:26:23.246 --> 00:26:25.414
Cal Warren's remains were
incinerated with aviation gas.

548
00:26:26.170 --> 00:26:27.207
I didn't kill Cal.

549
00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:30.340
You know what. she lies a lot.
I don't think she can help it at all.

550
00:26:30.755 --> 00:26:33.588
- Here's my lawyer's card.
- She's decided not to cooperate.

551
00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:36.838
No. I've decided to watch
my son play lacrosse.

552
00:26:41.139 --> 00:26:43.473
Here's the surface
weather for Tuesday night

553
00:26:43.643 --> 00:26:46.126
when that nor'easter blew
the bones into that tree.

554
00:26:48.133 --> 00:26:50.720
Now. that red X. that's the tree.

555
00:26:51.359 --> 00:26:54.288
The bones must have
traveled along this vector.

556
00:26:56.346 --> 00:26:58.989
Now. given the duration of the
gust and the terrain obstacles.

557
00:26:59.530 --> 00:27:01.543
lift off must have happened
somewhere between

558
00:27:01.668 --> 00:27:04.286
here... and here.

559
00:27:04.630 --> 00:27:07.935
That's on the edge of Queen
Anne's and Kent County.

560
00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:10.455
Good job. excellent experiment.

561
00:27:10.580 --> 00:27:12.029
Don't thank me.

562
00:27:12.250 --> 00:27:13.816
Thank Max Brennan.

563
00:27:20.330 --> 00:27:22.049
How's it going there. Max?

564
00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:24.598
That's the last day with
my kids this afternoon.

565
00:27:24.931 --> 00:27:26.095
I'm toast.

566
00:27:26.220 --> 00:27:27.267
Cam fired you?

567
00:27:27.714 --> 00:27:29.555
No. no. Tempe fired me.

568
00:27:29.773 --> 00:27:32.606
And don't tell me she hasn't got the
authority. because. believe me.

569
00:27:33.503 --> 00:27:34.938
I feel fired.

570
00:27:35.717 --> 00:27:36.752
Sorry. Max.

571
00:27:37.210 --> 00:27:38.978
Can I ask you a question?

572
00:27:39.550 --> 00:27:40.352
Sure.

573
00:27:40.821 --> 00:27:42.207
You. are you...

574
00:27:42.780 --> 00:27:45.366
- Are you sleeping with my daughter?
- No.

575
00:27:45.940 --> 00:27:47.709
Why? Are you gay?

576
00:27:48.670 --> 00:27:50.499
- No.
- Is she not attractive enough?

577
00:27:51.001 --> 00:27:52.959
- Bones is beautiful.
- Is it because of me?

578
00:27:53.245 --> 00:27:55.705
Because I killed one man. and
we both know he deserved it.

579
00:27:55.830 --> 00:27:57.917
Right. just cut it out. Max.
I'll talk to her.

580
00:27:58.042 --> 00:28:00.245
Probably ain't gonna get
anywhere with her. but...

581
00:28:00.776 --> 00:28:02.996
- I'll talk to her.
- You're a good man.

582
00:28:04.270 --> 00:28:05.904
And I want that for her.

583
00:28:07.484 --> 00:28:10.396
And now I got to go blow
up some soda for some kids.

584
00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:18.525
Okay. according to the calculations.

585
00:28:18.650 --> 00:28:20.533
the bones must have started out

586
00:28:20.658 --> 00:28:23.321
from somewhere in this vicinity.

587
00:28:23.446 --> 00:28:26.383
You know something. Bones?
It's tough being a father.

588
00:28:26.730 --> 00:28:28.135
Parker will be fine.

589
00:28:28.260 --> 00:28:30.300
Peer groups
and random environmental factors

590
00:28:30.425 --> 00:28:32.453
are far more important than family.

591
00:28:32.578 --> 00:28:34.105
How's that a good thing?

592
00:28:34.337 --> 00:28:35.210
Over here!

593
00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:37.686
Agent Booth. over here.

594
00:28:42.098 --> 00:28:44.955
This must have been where
the... body was burned.

595
00:28:45.080 --> 00:28:46.219
You think?

596
00:28:46.588 --> 00:28:48.098
Femur. pelvis...

597
00:28:48.642 --> 00:28:49.652
sternum.

598
00:28:50.510 --> 00:28:52.769
Gunshot trauma to the sternal angle.

599
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:55.687
The buckshot embedded
in the anterior surface

600
00:28:55.812 --> 00:28:58.817
indicates that the murder weapon
was a 12-gauge shotgun.

601
00:29:01.570 --> 00:29:03.605
- I thought Cal was strangled.
- He was.

602
00:29:03.783 --> 00:29:05.751
Strangled. shot and set on fire.

603
00:29:06.326 --> 00:29:09.060
Someone wanted to make
sure he didn't get home.

604
00:29:10.110 --> 00:29:12.613
Hey. Bones.
look at the family crest.

605
00:29:13.510 --> 00:29:16.442
Looks like that someone came from
king's country home.

606
00:29:28.428 --> 00:29:31.731
Mr. King. we'd like to ask you a
few questions about your nanny.

607
00:29:32.627 --> 00:29:34.859
I really don't see how
I can help you. Agent Booth.

608
00:29:35.370 --> 00:29:37.115
My wife deals with the staff.

609
00:29:37.240 --> 00:29:38.780
You own a 12-gauge shotgun?

610
00:29:39.140 --> 00:29:40.310
Yeah. several.

611
00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:42.645
You're welcome to examine them.

612
00:29:42.770 --> 00:29:44.479
Two months ago. Cal gave

613
00:29:44.604 --> 00:29:47.205
an investor insider knowledge
about your company.

614
00:29:47.450 --> 00:29:49.492
- I didn't know that.
- And if you had known?

615
00:29:50.042 --> 00:29:51.876
I suppose I would
have tried to fire him.

616
00:29:52.380 --> 00:29:53.180
Tried?

617
00:29:53.305 --> 00:29:55.467
I don't think that
Elsbeth would have allowed it.

618
00:29:55.592 --> 00:29:57.215
Was she having an affair with him?

619
00:29:57.383 --> 00:29:59.509
Oh. Bones. such a good one.

620
00:29:59.964 --> 00:30:02.011
You two need to learn focus.

621
00:30:02.371 --> 00:30:04.255
- Excuse me?
- Focus. Focus.

622
00:30:04.432 --> 00:30:06.278
Either accuse me
of killing Cal because

623
00:30:06.403 --> 00:30:09.060
he betrayed business secrets
or because he had sex with my wife.

624
00:30:09.230 --> 00:30:11.980
and then once you've
chosen. then contact my lawyers.

625
00:30:12.387 --> 00:30:14.105
I'd go with the business motive.

626
00:30:14.230 --> 00:30:15.824
I'm very happily married.

627
00:30:22.240 --> 00:30:24.000
Okay. that guy is one cool customer.

628
00:30:24.698 --> 00:30:26.235
Cool like a murderer?

629
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:28.005
No. I don't know. okay?

630
00:30:28.130 --> 00:30:30.274
I just don't see him
losing his temper

631
00:30:30.399 --> 00:30:32.792
or taking on some
Special Forces vet. that's all.

632
00:30:33.840 --> 00:30:36.398
All right. do you think that
dog comes with a saddle?

633
00:30:40.315 --> 00:30:42.470
Follow me. Bones.
will you. for a second?

634
00:30:46.760 --> 00:30:47.805
What's going on?

635
00:30:48.387 --> 00:30:49.898
What are you doing?

636
00:30:52.805 --> 00:30:55.440
Are you going to urinate in the
gas tank as an act of vandalism?

637
00:30:55.890 --> 00:30:58.407
You kidding me. Bones? I would never
do something like that

638
00:30:58.532 --> 00:31:00.668
to this fine Italian automobile.

639
00:31:02.499 --> 00:31:04.030
Beautiful car. It's Italian. Bones.

640
00:31:04.155 --> 00:31:07.201
Just remember that. Italians
make the best automobiles.

641
00:31:09.415 --> 00:31:10.723
Yeah. There it is.

642
00:31:13.803 --> 00:31:16.252
Okay. Bones. give me. one
of your little baggies.

643
00:31:16.422 --> 00:31:18.577
- I didn't bring evidence bags.
- Thanks. Appreciate it.

644
00:31:18.702 --> 00:31:20.855
We're not at a crime scene.
Why would I bring this bags?

645
00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:22.880
You always have
evidence bags on you.

646
00:31:24.796 --> 00:31:25.746
I've...

647
00:31:26.206 --> 00:31:28.405
I've decided
I'm gonna leave the Jeffersonian.

648
00:31:28.530 --> 00:31:29.360
Why?

649
00:31:29.485 --> 00:31:30.683
Because I fired him.

650
00:31:31.370 --> 00:31:34.312
- You can do that?
- Yeah. Believe me. she can do it.

651
00:31:34.780 --> 00:31:37.615
Well. it's all about proximity
to forensic evidence.

652
00:31:37.818 --> 00:31:40.091
Don't take any offense. but
that's a lot of crap.

653
00:31:40.653 --> 00:31:43.029
It's about proximity to me. Right?

654
00:31:46.207 --> 00:31:47.567
Well. in my opinion.

655
00:31:47.692 --> 00:31:50.595
it isn't your father's presence
that's causing you anxiety.

656
00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:53.081
it's the memory of his absence.

657
00:31:53.610 --> 00:31:57.043
I can understand quantum
mechanics. but I can't understand you.

658
00:31:57.760 --> 00:32:00.672
Well. make it easy.
I'm leaving the Jeffersonian.

659
00:32:01.954 --> 00:32:02.757
You are?

660
00:32:05.061 --> 00:32:08.073
- But I'm staying with you.
- What? In my house?

661
00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:09.931
No. no. no.

662
00:32:10.254 --> 00:32:11.516
Why. is that an offer?

663
00:32:11.684 --> 00:32:12.891
No. Would you...

664
00:32:13.324 --> 00:32:15.043
Would you want me to offer?

665
00:32:15.260 --> 00:32:16.771
No. but thanks for the offer.

666
00:32:16.939 --> 00:32:18.690
It wasn't an offer.
It was a question.

667
00:32:19.092 --> 00:32:21.512
He isn't saying he's
literally staying with you.

668
00:32:21.791 --> 00:32:23.694
He's promising never
to abandon you again.

669
00:32:28.200 --> 00:32:30.447
I'm sorry. but if it wasn't for that
evidence thing.

670
00:32:30.572 --> 00:32:31.994
I'd let you keep your job.

671
00:32:32.659 --> 00:32:34.315
That's simply not true.

672
00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:35.873
Hey. it's all right.

673
00:32:37.510 --> 00:32:38.710
We're good.

674
00:32:40.409 --> 00:32:42.380
Nothing I say has any impact.

675
00:32:43.099 --> 00:32:44.799
I should get back to work.

676
00:32:46.009 --> 00:32:46.860
Oh. geez.

677
00:32:50.704 --> 00:32:52.389
Did she leave any money?

678
00:32:59.017 --> 00:33:01.179
- About the fractured hyoid...
- Yes?

679
00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:04.618
I was just remembering
about a tapeworm.

680
00:33:05.654 --> 00:33:08.285
- I going to need more than that.
- There was a tapeworm in the line.

681
00:33:08.410 --> 00:33:10.095
The one that went to the beer keg.

682
00:33:11.535 --> 00:33:13.505
I was working as a
barback a couple years ago.

683
00:33:13.630 --> 00:33:16.581
There's no flow from the tap line.
First assumption: kink in the line. OK?

684
00:33:16.998 --> 00:33:18.291
What else could it be?

685
00:33:18.459 --> 00:33:20.335
There was a tapeworm in the line.

686
00:33:20.460 --> 00:33:21.735
Eight inches long.

687
00:33:21.860 --> 00:33:24.172
- I learned something from that.
- Drink bottled beer?

688
00:33:24.870 --> 00:33:27.950
The tap don't flow. you
assume the line's got a kink.

689
00:33:28.594 --> 00:33:32.597
The guy's hyoid is broken. you assume
he died from getting strangled.

690
00:33:32.900 --> 00:33:34.480
You found a tapeworm?

691
00:33:35.017 --> 00:33:36.309
I mean. metaphorically?

692
00:33:36.477 --> 00:33:38.265
Yeah. but I don't know
if it's a tapeworm.

693
00:33:38.390 --> 00:33:39.517
I need Dr. Brennan.

694
00:33:41.215 --> 00:33:43.434
I am so your most valuable player.

695
00:33:44.570 --> 00:33:47.361
Now. this is the profile of the
accelerant we found on the bones.

696
00:33:47.531 --> 00:33:48.490
Aviation gas.

697
00:33:48.615 --> 00:33:51.657
And this is the profile of the
gas we took off Booth's tie.

698
00:33:53.523 --> 00:33:55.244
Richard King's car runs on avgas?

699
00:33:55.414 --> 00:33:58.645
He could have siphoned it out of his
own car to burn Cal Warren's remains.

700
00:33:58.770 --> 00:34:00.415
And what is this anomaly?

701
00:34:00.615 --> 00:34:02.409
C6H8O7.

702
00:34:02.950 --> 00:34:04.195
Citric acid?

703
00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:08.132
It's my considered belief that Agent
Booth spilled orange juice on his tie.

704
00:34:08.514 --> 00:34:10.658
I look forward to seeing
him explain that to the jury.

705
00:34:10.783 --> 00:34:12.020
Booth. it's Cam.

706
00:34:12.145 --> 00:34:14.235
I think you're going to want
to getyourself a warrant

707
00:34:14.360 --> 00:34:16.000
to arrest Richard King.

708
00:34:17.630 --> 00:34:20.269
Fractures
on the transverse processes of the C2.

709
00:34:20.687 --> 00:34:22.647
both sides. and the spinous process.

710
00:34:22.815 --> 00:34:24.975
And check out the
occipital protuberance.

711
00:34:25.100 --> 00:34:25.975
Oh. yes.

712
00:34:26.100 --> 00:34:28.668
Maybe this will help Booth
keep Richard King in detention.

713
00:34:28.908 --> 00:34:31.115
Cal wasn't strangled postmortem.

714
00:34:31.240 --> 00:34:32.532
He was dragged.

715
00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:36.118
Strangulation is the kink.
dragging is the tapeworm.

716
00:34:37.060 --> 00:34:39.200
The pattern of marks
is evenly spaced as if

717
00:34:39.325 --> 00:34:41.290
it were from a series
of connected prongs.

718
00:34:41.560 --> 00:34:43.187
What would do that?

719
00:34:43.442 --> 00:34:44.910
A choke chain.

720
00:34:45.447 --> 00:34:47.133
Richard King's a big strong guy.

721
00:34:47.258 --> 00:34:49.685
I don't see him dragging a dead
body around on a choke chain.

722
00:34:49.810 --> 00:34:51.191
That's because he didn't.

723
00:34:51.980 --> 00:34:54.554
The angle of the fracture
is 18 degrees.

724
00:34:54.722 --> 00:34:57.165
Assuming a standard four-foot leash.
whoever dragged

725
00:34:57.290 --> 00:34:59.308
the victim is at most five-five.

726
00:35:09.830 --> 00:35:12.530
So. you're sure you don't want
your attorney present. Mrs. King?

727
00:35:12.660 --> 00:35:15.575
- Let's just get this over with.
- Okay. sounds good to me.

728
00:35:16.060 --> 00:35:18.025
Here's. what I'm thinking.

729
00:35:18.150 --> 00:35:19.680
I'm thinking that.

730
00:35:19.805 --> 00:35:21.790
your country home
is less than a mile

731
00:35:22.224 --> 00:35:24.215
from the spot where
Cal's body was burned.

732
00:35:24.340 --> 00:35:27.857
You had access to the
shotgun. the aviation gas...

733
00:35:28.050 --> 00:35:30.780
You know how many people
work for us. Agent Booth?

734
00:35:31.090 --> 00:35:32.710
Every single one of them had access.

735
00:35:32.835 --> 00:35:35.922
Yeah. I don't think any of them really
would have cared if they found out that.

736
00:35:36.047 --> 00:35:39.682
Cal Warren was trying to
destroy your husband's company.

737
00:35:45.770 --> 00:35:47.230
You have a nice life.

738
00:35:48.567 --> 00:35:52.361
I'm sure you got really angry when you
found out that it was all going away.

739
00:35:57.309 --> 00:35:58.900
You don't understand.

740
00:35:59.480 --> 00:36:01.280
It wasn't about the money.

741
00:36:02.804 --> 00:36:04.664
I had to protect my family.

742
00:36:08.206 --> 00:36:09.462
What do you think?

743
00:36:10.183 --> 00:36:12.805
In my professional
opinion. she didn't whack him.

744
00:36:12.930 --> 00:36:15.085
What? Come on. Cal betrayed them.

745
00:36:15.210 --> 00:36:17.610
Come on. Sweets.
For once. you're right.

746
00:36:17.919 --> 00:36:21.223
- Embrace the win. my friend.
- I'm sorry. but it's Kinesics 101.

747
00:36:21.820 --> 00:36:23.470
You pushed all the right buttons.

748
00:36:23.595 --> 00:36:26.604
but instead of her ego defense system
triggering a stress-response state.

749
00:36:26.872 --> 00:36:28.793
she went straight into
a tacit confession.

750
00:36:28.918 --> 00:36:31.525
Right. which means... she did it.

751
00:36:31.777 --> 00:36:33.605
No. it means she didn't do it.

752
00:36:33.970 --> 00:36:35.905
But she wants you to
believe that she did.

753
00:36:36.220 --> 00:36:38.077
Why would she want to do that?

754
00:36:38.416 --> 00:36:39.742
She's covering for someone.

755
00:36:40.083 --> 00:36:43.412
The only honest thing that she said
was that she had to protect her family.

756
00:36:43.730 --> 00:36:45.520
So we're back to square one.

757
00:36:45.690 --> 00:36:46.457
Sort of.

758
00:36:48.289 --> 00:36:49.070
Geez.

759
00:36:52.483 --> 00:36:54.220
Let me ask you something.

760
00:36:54.520 --> 00:36:56.842
I mean. you're a smart guy.
you went to private school. right?

761
00:36:57.012 --> 00:36:59.893
Yeah. With perfect attendance
through sixth grade. might I add.

762
00:37:00.018 --> 00:37:01.254
That's great.

763
00:37:02.943 --> 00:37:05.163
You don't think that
I'm a lousy dad for not

764
00:37:05.288 --> 00:37:07.144
sending my son to private school?

765
00:37:07.457 --> 00:37:08.312
No.

766
00:37:08.875 --> 00:37:12.108
but you'd be a lousy father if
you didn't torture yourself about it.

767
00:37:14.767 --> 00:37:15.585
Thanks.

768
00:37:18.047 --> 00:37:19.407
Hold on. Booth.

769
00:37:19.734 --> 00:37:22.638
I reviewed the placement of
the shotgun pellet wounds.

770
00:37:23.230 --> 00:37:25.767
The trajectory indicates that
whoever shot Cal

771
00:37:26.298 --> 00:37:28.541
was significantly
shorter than Mrs. King.

772
00:37:29.660 --> 00:37:32.508
- I don't think she did it.
- Right. thanks.

773
00:37:44.501 --> 00:37:48.215
You see. we got a court order
for your cell phone and your laptop.

774
00:37:48.340 --> 00:37:52.273
You know nothing you text
or IM is really private.

775
00:37:52.720 --> 00:37:53.760
I knew that.

776
00:37:54.057 --> 00:37:56.610
Really? Because. you know.
we checked your text messages. and.

777
00:37:57.380 --> 00:38:00.364
we found one from a couple
weeks ago that's a little weird.

778
00:38:00.790 --> 00:38:03.325
This one is from the
night that Cal was killed.

779
00:38:03.495 --> 00:38:05.870
"Bring it over now.
Parents both gone."

780
00:38:06.038 --> 00:38:08.497
- Stop this. Richard.
- No. I want to hear it.

781
00:38:09.008 --> 00:38:11.834
It turns out that Alexa. here.
had a project due on Ancient Greece.

782
00:38:12.928 --> 00:38:14.798
You spent three days
complaining about it.

783
00:38:14.923 --> 00:38:17.023
- Why didn't you just do it?
- I didn't want to.

784
00:38:17.224 --> 00:38:19.027
- It was stupid.
- Stupid?

785
00:38:20.130 --> 00:38:22.405
- How about this one?
- "D manny will do it.

786
00:38:22.530 --> 00:38:24.722
He can't say no. He works for me."

787
00:38:25.510 --> 00:38:27.175
But Cal really did say no.
didn't he?

788
00:38:27.300 --> 00:38:30.035
Because you paid a hundred bucks
to somebody else to do it for you.

789
00:38:30.160 --> 00:38:32.563
Someone by the name
of Dakota Shearcroft.

790
00:38:33.717 --> 00:38:36.775
Oh. my God.
Yeah. I think it's a stupid name. too.

791
00:38:36.900 --> 00:38:39.195
So what happened?
Did Cal catch you?

792
00:38:39.562 --> 00:38:41.238
He threatened to tell the school.

793
00:38:41.408 --> 00:38:44.283
- Why wouldn't he have just told us?
- Cal said you wouldn't do anything.

794
00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:46.511
You never do.

795
00:38:47.122 --> 00:38:49.830
- He said I had to learn a lesson.
- What kind of lesson?

796
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:52.875
They would have kicked me
out of school! Zero tolerance.

797
00:38:55.785 --> 00:38:57.505
My friends are at that school.

798
00:38:59.940 --> 00:39:02.009
I got the gun out of the garage
and I shot him.

799
00:39:05.880 --> 00:39:07.097
Mom came home and saw.

800
00:39:12.220 --> 00:39:14.396
I drove the body to the country
house.

801
00:39:15.084 --> 00:39:17.341
took it into the woods
and burned it.

802
00:39:22.830 --> 00:39:25.328
She's my daughter.
I had to protect her.

803
00:39:26.352 --> 00:39:28.160
No. you did what you always do.

804
00:39:28.564 --> 00:39:29.995
Make everything bad go away.

805
00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:34.124
It's counterproductive to raise children
in a world without consequences.

806
00:39:34.294 --> 00:39:36.961
It looks like little Alexa here
is going to have to come face-to-face

807
00:39:37.129 --> 00:39:40.005
with some pretty nasty consequences.

808
00:39:40.389 --> 00:39:44.218
But not the kind of consequences
you're going to have to face. Mrs. King.

809
00:39:55.948 --> 00:39:58.645
Okay. Parker. this is called
the candy mint-soda experiment.

810
00:39:58.819 --> 00:40:00.860
You can do this
for your dad at home.

811
00:40:01.281 --> 00:40:04.305
So. Mom copped to
conspiracy to avoid a trial.

812
00:40:04.430 --> 00:40:06.915
- She'll spend some time in prison.
- How much?

813
00:40:07.040 --> 00:40:09.660
Not enough. My opinion.
she ruined that little girl's life.

814
00:40:11.212 --> 00:40:12.739
What about the little girl?

815
00:40:12.864 --> 00:40:15.666
Removed from the family.
institutionalized for a couple of years.

816
00:40:17.481 --> 00:40:20.360
Then it's back to ponies
and tennis lessons?

817
00:40:21.340 --> 00:40:23.674
Well. Caroline should
charge her as an adult.

818
00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:25.968
She's 11 years old. Bones.

819
00:40:26.136 --> 00:40:27.887
Yeah. she's old
enough to speak Chinese.

820
00:40:28.055 --> 00:40:29.865
They don't take that into account.

821
00:40:30.600 --> 00:40:34.714
Man. when that little girl killed Cal
she killed the best father she had.

822
00:40:35.512 --> 00:40:38.107
Well. sometimes it's hard
to appreciate what you've got.

823
00:40:40.640 --> 00:40:43.435
Look at him. Parker
has never liked science before.

824
00:40:43.936 --> 00:40:46.113
Are you still thinking of
sending him to Woodbury?

825
00:40:47.146 --> 00:40:48.635
I torched the application.

826
00:40:48.760 --> 00:40:51.243
I'm thinking there's something
to be said for middle class.

827
00:40:53.882 --> 00:40:55.735
You sure he's going to be all right?

828
00:40:56.053 --> 00:40:58.440
Sure. Well. probably.

829
00:40:59.086 --> 00:41:01.698
Probably. like.
what do you mean. probably?

830
00:41:01.823 --> 00:41:03.495
What the hell
are they doing anyways?

831
00:41:03.620 --> 00:41:06.375
Disrupting the surface
tension of a two-liter cola.

832
00:41:08.230 --> 00:41:09.031
Right.

833
00:41:10.320 --> 00:41:12.595
Is that the last one?All
right. put it in the tube.

834
00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:14.467
And then we'll both
take a step back.

835
00:41:15.510 --> 00:41:17.675
Don't fire Max.
Let him keep his job.

836
00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:19.355
He's a teacher. he's not a janitor.

837
00:41:19.714 --> 00:41:23.118
I can't overlook the sanctity
of the forensic lab. Booth.

838
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:26.625
Yeah.
maybe you can overlook it for me.

839
00:41:27.598 --> 00:41:28.572
For you?

840
00:41:29.933 --> 00:41:30.771
Yeah.

841
00:41:30.896 --> 00:41:31.950
Personal favor.

842
00:41:32.636 --> 00:41:34.286
What. like a partner thing?

843
00:41:36.166 --> 00:41:37.401
A partner thing.

844
00:41:41.870 --> 00:41:43.185
I know you. Booth.

845
00:41:43.310 --> 00:41:46.173
You're trying to do me a favor
by telling me it's a favor for you.

846
00:41:46.343 --> 00:41:47.127
No.

847
00:41:48.268 --> 00:41:50.633
No. I...
I can't afford that school.

848
00:41:51.519 --> 00:41:54.832
I can't enrich Parker.
not with the science thing. but...

849
00:41:55.960 --> 00:41:57.276
you can. Max can.

850
00:42:06.862 --> 00:42:07.901
Do it again.

851
00:42:08.456 --> 00:42:10.614
Daddy! Daddy. look what I did!
I blew it up!

852
00:42:10.964 --> 00:42:12.241
Yeah. I saw little man.

853
00:42:18.888 --> 00:42:19.999
Look at my dad!

854
00:42:23.485 --> 00:42:26.510
Look at my boy there with your dad.

855
00:42:31.621 --> 00:42:32.381
Okay.

856
00:42:34.250 --> 00:42:35.134
Yes...

857
00:42:36.261 --> 00:42:38.017
- All right.
- Thanks. Bones.
